.\" Manpage for krl-client. Render:  man ./packaging/krl-client.8
.\" Install:  install -Dm0644 packaging/krl-client.8 /usr/local/share/man/man8/krl-client.8
.TH KRL-CLIENT 8 "2026-07-02" "krl-client" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
krl-client \- fetch, decrypt, verify and install this host's OpenSSH KRL from PKI Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krl-client
.B \-\-server-url
.I URL
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B krl-client keygen
[\fB\-\-out\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR \fIC\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B krl-client \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B krl-client
keeps a machine's OpenSSH key-revocation list current. Each run POSTs the
per-host encrypted endpoint
.RB ( /api/v1/external/ssh/krl ),
decrypts the payload
.B locally
with the host's own
.B ecdsa-sha2-nistp256
key (the private key never leaves the box; the KMS is never contacted),
verifies the CA's detached signature, checks the payload's host_id, expiry and
anti-rollback counter, and
.B atomically
installs the KRL at the sshd
.B RevokedKeys
path (0444 root:root). It is a oneshot: it runs one cycle and exits with a code
that a cron or systemd-timer wrapper can alert on.
.PP
A conditional request is made with
.BR If-None-Match :
the token is the server's
.I krl_version
(the value cached from the previous run's
.B X-KRL-Version
response header), not a hash of the local file. When the host already holds the
current KRL the server returns 304 and the run is a no-op (exit 0).
.PP
On a host provisioned from PKI Manager's per-host deploy bundle (or the
Ansible role) — which installs the Host-CA trust anchor at
.I /etc/ssh/ssh-host-ca.pub
— every on-host path default already matches, so the only required flag is
.BR \-\-server-url .
.SH OPTIONS
Each option may also be set via an environment variable
.RB ( KRL_CLIENT_ " + the flag name upper-cased, " \- " to " _ )
or a flat-YAML config-file key (the flag name verbatim). Precedence, highest
first: flag > environment > config file > built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-server-url " URL"
PKI Manager base URL.
.BR Required .
.TP
.BI \-\-host-id " FQDN"
Host FQDN sent in the request body. Default:
.BR "hostname \-f" .
.TP
.BI \-\-host-key " PATH"
ECDSA private key used for local ECIES decryption. Default:
.IR /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ecdsa_key .
.TP
.BI \-\-ca-pubkey " PATH"
Host-CA public key for detached-signature verification (the server signs the
composed per-host KRL with the Host-CA key). Default:
.IR /etc/ssh/ssh-host-ca.pub .
.TP
.BI \-\-krl-file " PATH"
Install target (sshd RevokedKeys). Default:
.IR /etc/ssh/revoked_keys .
.TP
.BI \-\-state-dir " PATH"
Version/state cache directory. Default:
.IR /var/lib/krl-client .
.TP
.BI \-\-ca-bundle " PATH"
TLS CA bundle (PEM) pinning the server. Default: system roots.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Disable TLS verification (DANGEROUS; dev only). Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-ca-bundle .
While in effect, a
.B WARN
event
.RB ( event=insecure_tls )
is logged on every run \(em surfacing even under
.B \-\-quiet
\(em so the host is never silently left unverified.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-unsigned
Install even when the payload
.I ca_signature
is null.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DUR"
Per-request timeout. Default:
.BR 30s .
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Retries on network errors / 5xx. Default:
.BR 3 .
.TP
.BI \-\-max-response-bytes " N"
Maximum accepted size, in bytes, of the encrypted KRL response body. An oversized
response fails closed (exit
.BR 2 )
rather than being buffered into memory. Default:
.BR 8388608 " (8 MiB)."
.TP
.BI \-\-clock-skew " DUR"
Leeway when checking payload
.IR valid_until .
Default:
.BR 300s .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Fetch, decrypt and verify but do not write the KRL file.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Log warnings and errors only; a successful run is silent (cron-friendly).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log per-step debug detail. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-quiet .
.TP
.BI \-\-log-format " text|json"
Log format. Default:
.BR text .
.TP
.B \-\-systemd
systemd integration; implies
.BR \-\-log-format=json " with no ANSI."
.TP
.B \-\-oneshot
Run one cycle and exit (the current default behaviour).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Config-file path. Default:
.IR /etc/krl-client/config.yaml .
.RB "(env: " KRL_CLIENT_CONFIG )
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version to stdout and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TS
l l.
0	up-to-date (304) or a newer KRL verified and installed
1	usage / configuration error
2	network \(en DNS/connect/TLS/timeout, retries exhausted, or 5xx
3	local ECIES decryption failed
4	CA signature verification failed
5	payload expired (valid_until in the past beyond clock-skew)
6	host mismatch (payload host_id != our host-id)
7	atomic install of the KRL file failed
8	version / integrity / anti-rollback failure
9	not provisioned / feature disabled (400/404/501)
10	rate limited (429) \(en back off and retry later
.TE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRL_CLIENT_SERVER_URL
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-server-url .
Every other flag has the same
.BR KRL_CLIENT_ *
form.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ecdsa_key
Default ECIES decryption key (read only; never transmitted).
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/ssh-host-ca.pub
Default CA public key for signature verification (the Host CA trust anchor
installed by the pki-manager Ansible role).
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/revoked_keys
Default install target (sshd RevokedKeys).
.TP
.I /var/lib/krl-client
Version/anti-rollback state cache.
.TP
.I /etc/krl-client/config.yaml
Optional flat-YAML config file.
.SH NOTES
.B A synced clock is a hard prerequisite.
The client rejects a payload whose
.I valid_until
is in the past beyond
.BR \-\-clock-skew ;
a machine whose clock has drifted will fail every run. Keep NTP running.
.PP
After the KRL is installed it is effective immediately: sshd re-reads
.B RevokedKeys
on every authentication attempt — no reload or restart is needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sshd_config (5)
.RB ( RevokedKeys ),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
.RB ( \-k / \-Q " KRL tooling), " systemd.timer (5).
The full README ships at
.IR krl-client/README.md .
